# 5. TUTOR DATA SECURITY

This is one of the most important requirements.

A tutor must only access data they are authorized to access.

A tutor can generally access:

```text
Their own Tutor profile
Their own Assignments
Students assigned to them
Parents related to their assigned students
Their own Sessions
Their own Attendance records
Their own Schedule
Their own Tutor Payables
Their own Tutor Payments
Authorized Conversations
Their own Notifications
Their own Preferences
Their own Account Settings
```

A tutor must NOT access:

```text
Another tutor's assignments
Another tutor's students
Another tutor's payables
Another tutor's payments
Another tutor's private messages
Internal staff conversations
CRM leads
Internal tutor matching scores
Other tutors' commissions
Other tutors' personal information
Other parents' unrelated information
```

---

# 6. TENANT ISOLATION

Every Tutor Portal API must enforce organization isolation.

The backend must derive:

```text
organizationId
```

from authenticated context.

Never trust:

```text
organizationId
```

from request body/query parameters.

Conceptually:

```text
Authenticated User
        ↓
Resolve Tutor
        ↓
Tutor.organizationId
        ↓
Verify req.auth.organizationId
        ↓
Query Tutor-owned resources
```

Cross-tenant access must be impossible.

